From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:47:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11.drv: Run Mesa without its threaded context
 unless told otherwise.

Not intended for upstream: a workaround until Mesa is fixed.

Mesa's gallium threaded context walks the contexts that share state when
it releases a buffer, and _mesa_initialize_context() puts a context on
that list before st_create_context_priv() gives it an st_context.  A
thread releasing a buffer meanwhile dereferences the NULL st with the
shared state's mutex held; the fault inside the unix call is returned as
a status, the mutex stays locked, and every GL thread of the process
hangs.  With every context shared with a root context, Office hits it
whenever one thread makes a Direct3D device while another draws: Word
at start-up, Excel when it is activated in place in Word (the fix for
Mesa is in wine-altars' patches/mesa).

GALLIUM_THREAD=0 takes the threaded context away, and with it the walk.
Measured with Office: Word started hung 5 times in 7 before, embedding
Excel in Word hung once in 2; with the driver unthreaded, none of 5 and
none of 4.  Setting GALLIUM_THREAD in the environment still wins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/opengl.c b/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
index 5267f75b711..630301d6f64 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/opengl.c
@@ -1587,6 +1587,14 @@ static BOOL egl_init( const struct opengl_driver_funcs **driver_funcs )
     struct opengl_funcs *funcs = &display_funcs;
     const char *str;
 
+    /* Not intended for upstream.  Mesa's gallium threaded context walks the contexts that share
+     * state when it releases a buffer, and a context another thread is still creating is on that
+     * list before it can be walked; the fault leaves the shared state locked and every GL thread
+     * of the process hangs (patches/mesa in wine-altars).  With every context shared with a root
+     * one, Office hits it whenever one thread makes a Direct3D device while another draws.  Unless
+     * told otherwise, the driver runs without its threaded context. */
+    setenv( "GALLIUM_THREAD", "0", 0 );
+
     if (!(funcs->egl_handle = dlopen( SONAME_LIBEGL, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL )))
     {
         ERR( "Failed to load %s: %s\n", SONAME_LIBEGL, dlerror() );
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
index a9a2bd73791..1bf4a96e04e 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/opengl.c
@@ -580,6 +580,9 @@ UINT X11DRV_OpenGLInit( UINT version, const struct opengl_funcs *opengl_funcs, c
 
     use_egl = FALSE;
 
+    /* Not intended for upstream: without Mesa's threaded context, as win32u does for EGL */
+    setenv( "GALLIUM_THREAD", "0", 0 );
+
     /* No need to load any other libraries as according to the ABI, libGL should be self-sufficient
        and include all dependencies */
     opengl_handle = dlopen( SONAME_LIBGL, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL );
